@page
@model BeeMemoryBank.Web.Pages.Admin.DreamModel

@* Dream settings (plan 3.9) - superadmin-only (the whole area is). The form is read and saved by dream-admin.js through /api-proxy/dream (plan 3.8). *@
@section About {
    <p>
        <strong>Dream</strong> (in the header, after Search) looks through the notes of this node and leaves advice on keeping them in order:
        duplicates, notes in the wrong folder, tags spelled several ways, empty folders. It changes nothing by itself; every change is made by a
        person pressing a button on the Dream page. This page decides what a run may do: when the nightly run is allowed, how much advice it may
        leave, whether a model may take part, which folders Dream never reads, and what has been dismissed for good.
    </p>
    <p class="admin-warning">
        <strong>With a model switched on, note content leaves this node.</strong> Dream sends the text of every note it looks at - all notes of the
        node except those under a second password and those in the excluded folders below - through OpenRouter to the model chosen in the Model
        section. With the model off, Dream works from local rules alone and nothing leaves the node.
    </p>
    <p>
        The nightly schedule and these limits belong to <strong>this node alone</strong>: with several full nodes, turn the schedule on on one of
        them, or each node will spend its own budget and keep its own list of advice. Dream runs only while the vault is unlocked; it never unlocks
        anything itself.
    </p>
}

<div id="dream-settings">
    @* The script fills this when the node does not serve the Dream settings yet (it answers "not implemented"): the form then
       shows the planned defaults and Save stays off until the node's Dream service arrives (package P0b of the plan). *@
    <div id="dream-endpoint-note" hidden aria-live="polite"></div>

    <h3 style="margin-bottom:12px;"><sl-icon name="moon-stars"></sl-icon> Schedule</h3>
    <div class="card" style="padding:16px;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:24px;">
        <sl-switch id="dream-schedule-enabled" size="small">Run nightly</sl-switch>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin:8px 0 16px 0;">
            When it is on, Dream starts once a night inside the window below, if the vault is unlocked, nothing heavy is going on and the list of
            open advice is not full.
        </p>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:16px;">
            <sl-input id="dream-schedule-start" size="small" label="Window opens at (node-local HH:mm)" placeholder="03:00"></sl-input>
            <sl-input id="dream-schedule-window" type="number" min="15" max="720" size="small" label="Window length (minutes)"></sl-input>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-bottom:12px;"><sl-icon name="sliders"></sl-icon> Limits</h3>
    <div class="card" style="padding:16px;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:24px;">
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:16px;">
            <sl-input id="dream-max-advice-scheduled" type="number" min="1" max="500" size="small"
                      label="New advice per nightly run" help-text="10 by default; 50 and more is fine."></sl-input>
            <sl-input id="dream-max-advice-manual" type="number" min="0" max="1000" size="small"
                      label="New advice per manual run" help-text="0 = no limit."></sl-input>
            <sl-input id="dream-max-open-advice" type="number" min="1" max="10000" size="small"
                      label="Open advice before a nightly run is skipped" help-text="At this many undecided advice the night skips."></sl-input>
            <sl-input id="dream-min-score" type="number" min="0" max="100" size="small"
                      label="Lowest score kept (0-100)" help-text="Advice scoring below this is not kept."></sl-input>
            <sl-input id="dream-manual-max-minutes" type="number" min="0" max="1440" size="small"
                      label="Manual run time limit (minutes)" help-text="0 = no limit."></sl-input>
            <sl-input id="dream-max-model-calls" type="number" min="1" max="10000" size="small"
                      label="Model calls per run"></sl-input>
            <sl-input id="dream-max-tokens" type="number" min="1000" max="100000000" size="small"
                      label="Tokens per run (input + output)"></sl-input>
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin:12px 0 0 0;">
            The limits of a run are fixed when it starts: changing them here does not change a run that is going on.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-bottom:12px;"><sl-icon name="cpu"></sl-icon> Model</h3>
    <div class="card" style="padding:16px;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:24px;">
        <sl-switch id="dream-use-model" size="small">Use a model</sl-switch>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin:8px 0 16px 0;">
            With it off, Dream runs on local rules alone and <strong>nothing leaves this node</strong>. With it on, every run also asks the model:
            the text of every note it looks at - except the protected ones and the excluded folders below - goes through OpenRouter to the model
            chosen here, and what the model advises is kept on this node like every other advice. OpenRouter keys and models are managed on the
            <a href="/Admin/AiChat">AI / Chat</a> page.
        </p>
        <label style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-secondary);display:block;margin-bottom:4px;">Model for Dream</label>
        <sl-select id="dream-analysis-model" size="small" style="max-width:360px;" hoist></sl-select>
        <p id="dream-models-hint" class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin:8px 0 0 0;"></p>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-bottom:12px;"><sl-icon name="folder-x"></sl-icon> Excluded folders</h3>
    <div class="card" style="padding:16px;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:24px;">
        <p class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin:0 0 12px 0;">
            Dream never reads these folders, sends their notes nowhere and never mentions them. One path per line, e.g. <code>/Imported</code>. The
            node turns the paths into folders when you save; a path it does not know refuses the save.
        </p>
        <sl-textarea id="dream-excluded-folders" rows="4" placeholder="/Imported" style="max-width:480px;"></sl-textarea>
    </div>

    <div style="margin:0 0 32px 0;">
        <sl-button id="btn-save-dream-settings" variant="primary" size="small">
            <sl-icon slot="prefix" name="save"></sl-icon> Save settings
        </sl-button>
        <span id="dream-settings-updated" class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin-left:8px;"></span>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-bottom:8px;"><sl-icon name="x-circle"></sl-icon> Dismiss rules</h3>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin:0 0 8px 0;">
        Dismissing advice can leave a rule that keeps it - or every advice of its kind - from coming back on later runs. Delete a rule here to let
        Dream suggest it again.
    </p>
    <div class="card" style="padding:0;overflow:hidden;">
        @* The rows are built by dream-admin.js; they carry the classes and the data-label of the stacked layout (site.css, Admin): below a card
           of 560px a row stacks, nothing is hidden. *@
        <table class="version-table admin-stack-sm" id="dream-rules">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th class="col-name">Created</th>
                    <th>Scope</th>
                    <th>Kind</th>
                    <th>Applies to</th>
                    <th>Reason</th>
                    <th>Expires</th>
                    <th class="col-actions">Actions</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="dream-rules-body">
                <tr><td colspan="7" class="col-empty text-muted text-sm">Loading…</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>
